{"id":73,"attempt_id":"55740c4c-37ce-4cea-abee-4cb54bb5161b","title":"Solve the IVP:  dy/dx = y(1 - y),  y(0) = 0.2.\nTasks:\n1) Show the equation is se","subject":"Math","is_saved":true,"created_at":"2026-02-23T10:20:16.436051","messages":[{"id":137,"role":"user","content":"Solve the IVP:  dy/dx = y(1 - y),  y(0) = 0.2.\nTasks:\n1) Show the equation is separable.\n2) Separate variables and integrate.\n3) Solve for y(x) explicitly.\n4) Apply y(0)=0.2 to find the constant.\n5) State the final closed-form solution.\n6) Find equilibrium solutions and classify them (stable/unstable).\n7) Determine lim_{xââ} y(x).\n8) Find where the solution has its inflection point (in x).\n9) Compute the time x when y(x)=0.5.\n10) Compute the time x when y(x)=0.8.\n11) Verify y(0)=0.2 by direct substitution into your formula.\n12) Plot y(x) on x â [-5, 10].\n13) Overlay a slope field on the same window (coarse grid acceptable).\n14) Plot the phase line for y' = y(1-y) on the y-axis (direction arrows).\n15) Mark and label the points where y=0.5 and y=0.8 on the solution plot.","display_markdown":null,"rendered_content":null,"media_url":null,"structured_data":null,"created_at":"2026-02-23T10:20:16.439140","model_used":null,"tokens_used":0,"input_tokens":null,"output_tokens":null,"telemetry":null},{"id":138,"role":"assistant","content":"","display_markdown":"","rendered_content":"","media_url":null,"structured_data":{"attempt_id":"eea47c34-ee21-4858-8406-530a1fa0c885","context":{"country":null,"course":null,"curriculum":null,"grade_level":null,"notation_profile":null,"region":null},"items":[{"clarification":{"needs_clarification":false,"note":null,"questions":[]},"classification":{"detected_tasks":["solve","set_theory","differential_equations","equation","graph","plot","stability_analysis","calculus"],"domain":"differential_equations"},"domain_mode":"reals","final_answer":{"answer_latex":"\\displaystyle y(x)=\\frac{1}{1+4e^{-x}}","answer_text":"y(x) = 1/(1+4 e^{-x})","values":[{"key":"solution","latex":"\\displaystyle y(x)=\\frac{1}{1+4e^{-x}}","number":null,"text":"y(x)=1/(1+4 e^{-x})","unit":null}]},"plot":{"notes":null,"python_code":"import numpy as np\nimport matplotlib.pyplot as plt\nfrom math import exp\nx = np.linspace(-5,10,601)\ny = 1/(1+4*np.exp(-x))\n# slope field (coarse)\nX, Y = np.meshgrid(np.linspace(-5,10,16), np.linspace(-0.2,1.2,13))\nU = 1\nV = Y*(1-Y)\nN = np.hypot(U,V)\nU2, V2 = U/N, V/N\nplt.figure(figsize=(8,5))\nplt.quiver(X, Y, U2, V2, color='lightgray')\nplt.plot(x,y,'b-',label='y(x)')\nplt.plot(np.log(4),0.5,'ro',label='y=0.5 at x=ln4')\nplt.plot(np.log(16),0.8,'go',label='y=0.8 at x=ln16')\nplt.ylim(-0.1,1.1)\nplt.xlim(-5,10)\nplt.xlabel('x')\nplt.ylabel('y')\nplt.legend()\nplt.grid(True)\nplt.title('Solution, slope field, and markers')\n# Phase line (separate figure)\nplt.figure(figsize=(2,6))\nys = np.linspace(-0.2,1.2,200)\ndy = ys*(1-ys)\nplt.axhline(0,color='k')\nfor y0 in np.linspace(-0.1,1.1,10):\n    s = np.sign(y0*(1-y0))\n    plt.arrow(0,y0,0.3*s,0,head_width=0.02,head_length=0.05,color='k')\nplt.plot(0,0,'ro')\nplt.plot(0,1,'ro')\nplt.ylim(-0.2,1.2)\nplt.xlim(-0.5,0.8)\nplt.axis('off')\nplt.title('Phase line')\nplt.show()","recipe":{"axes_lines":true,"grid":true,"kind":"function_2d","legend":true,"points":[{"kind":"custom","label":"y=0.5 marker","x":1.3862943611198906,"y":0.5},{"kind":"custom","label":"y=0.8 marker","x":2.772588722239781,"y":0.8}],"series":[{"expr_latex":"\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{1+4e^{-x}}","kind":"function","label":"y(x)=1/(1+4e^{-x})","params":[],"samples":[],"series_id":"solution","variable":"x","x_expr_latex":null,"y_expr_latex":null}],"shapes":[],"title":"Solution y(x) with slope field and markers","x_domain":{"max":10,"min":-5},"x_label":"x","y_domain":{"max":1.2,"min":-0.1},"y_label":"y","layers":[{"layer_id":"slope_field","type":"slope_field","label":"slope field (coarse)","params":[{"latex":null,"name":"x_range","number":null,"text":"[-5,10]"},{"latex":null,"name":"y_range","number":null,"text":"[-0.2,1.2]"},{"latex":null,"name":"density","number":null,"text":"coarse"}]},{"layer_id":"phase_line","type":"annotation","label":"phase line (separate)","params":[]}]},"should_visualize":true,"decision_reason":"graph_mode_forced"},"quality":{"assumptions":["Standard logistic ODE on real x with initial condition y(0)=0.2","Plots use real-valued x in [-5,10]"],"confidence":0.95,"warnings":[]},"question_id":"q1","question_summary":"Solve logistic IVP dy/dx = y(1-y), y(0)=0.2; analyze and plot.","refusal":{"is_refusal":false,"refusal_code":null,"refusal_message":null},"results":{"task_results":[{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"Equation is separable: dy/(y(1-y)) = dx","task_index":1,"task_label":"Show separable"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"Integrate: ln(y/(1-y)) = x + C","task_index":2,"task_label":"Separate and integrate"},{"result_latex":"\\displaystyle y=\\frac{Ke^{x}}{1+Ke^{x}}","result_text":"General explicit solution y = K e^{x}/(1+K e^{x})","task_index":3,"task_label":"Solve explicitly"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"Using y(0)=0.2 gives K=1/4","task_index":4,"task_label":"Apply initial condition"},{"result_latex":"\\displaystyle y(x)=\\frac{1}{1+4e^{-x}}","result_text":"Final closed-form solution y(x)=1/(1+4 e^{-x})","task_index":5,"task_label":"Final solution"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"Equilibria: y=0 and y=1; y=0 unstable, y=1 stable","task_index":6,"task_label":"Equilibria & stability"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"lim_{xââ} y(x) = 1","task_index":7,"task_label":"Limit as xââ"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"Inflection occurs when y=1/2, which gives x=ln(4)","task_index":8,"task_label":"Inflection point"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"x when y=0.5: x=ln(4) â 1.38629","task_index":9,"task_label":"Time for y=0.5"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"x when y=0.8: x=ln(16) â 2.77259","task_index":10,"task_label":"Time for y=0.8"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"Verification: y(0)=1/(1+4)=1/5=0.2, matches initial condition","task_index":11,"task_label":"Verify initial condition"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"Plot specification and slope field provided; markers at y=0.5 and y=0.8 included","task_index":12,"task_label":"Plot y(x)"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"Slope field overlaid (coarse grid) on same plot","task_index":13,"task_label":"Overlay slope field"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"Phase line plotted with arrows; equilibria marked at y=0 and y=1","task_index":14,"task_label":"Phase line"},{"result_latex":null,"result_text":"Markers for y=0.5 and y=0.8 placed on solution plot at x=ln4 and x=ln16 respectively","task_index":15,"task_label":"Mark points on plot"}]},"steps":[{"blocks":[{"content":"The ODE dy/dx = y(1-y) is separable since the right-hand side factors into functions of y alone.","display":true,"kind":"text"}],"index":1,"title":"Show separable"},{"blocks":[{"content":"\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{y(1-y)}\\,dy=dx","display":true,"kind":"math"},{"content":"Integrate both sides.","display":true,"kind":"text"},{"content":"\\displaystyle \\int\\left(\\frac{1}{y} + \\frac{1}{1-y}\\right)dy = \\int dx","display":true,"kind":"math"},{"content":"\\displaystyle \\ln|y| - \\ln|1-y| = x + C","display":true,"kind":"math"}],"index":2,"title":"Separate and integrate"},{"blocks":[{"content":"\\displaystyle \\ln\\left(\\frac{y}{1-y}\\right)=x+C","display":true,"kind":"math"},{"content":"Exponentiate and solve for y.","display":true,"kind":"text"},{"content":"\\displaystyle \\frac{y}{1-y}=Ke^{x}\\quad\\Rightarrow\\quad y=\\frac{Ke^{x}}{1+Ke^{x}}","display":true,"kind":"math"}],"index":3,"title":"Solve for y explicitly"},{"blocks":[{"content":"Apply initial condition y(0)=0.2 to find K.","display":true,"kind":"text"},{"content":"\\displaystyle \\frac{0.2}{1-0.2}=\\frac{1}{4}=K","display":true,"kind":"math"},{"content":"\\displaystyle y(x)=\\frac{\\tfrac{1}{4}e^{x}}{1+\\tfrac{1}{4}e^{x}}=\\frac{1}{1+4e^{-x}}","display":true,"kind":"math"}],"index":4,"title":"Apply initial condition"},{"blocks":[{"content":"Final closed-form solution.","display":true,"kind":"text"},{"content":"\\displaystyle y(x)=\\frac{1}{1+4e^{-x}}","display":true,"kind":"math"}],"index":5,"title":"Final solution"},{"blocks":[{"content":"Equilibria occur where y'=0, i.e., y(1-y)=0, so y=0 and y=1. Linearization: f'(y)=1-2y gives f'(0)=1>0 (unstable), f'(1)=-1<0 (stable).","display":true,"kind":"text"}],"index":6,"title":"Equilibria and stability"},{"blocks":[{"content":"Limit as xââ.","display":true,"kind":"text"},{"content":"\\displaystyle \\lim_{x\\to\\infty}y(x)=1","display":true,"kind":"math"}],"index":7,"title":"Limit at infinity"},{"blocks":[{"content":"Inflection points when y''=0. Compute y'' = y'(1-2y) = y(1-y)(1-2y). So y''=0 when y=0,1, or y=1/2. The interior inflection is y=1/2.","display":true,"kind":"text"},{"content":"\\displaystyle y=\\tfrac{1}{2}","display":true,"kind":"math"}],"index":8,"title":"Inflection"},{"blocks":[{"content":"Solve y(x)=1/2: 1/(1+4e^{-x})=1/2 â 1+4e^{-x}=2 â e^{-x}=1/4 â x=\\ln 4.","display":true,"kind":"text"},{"content":"\\displaystyle x=\\ln 4\\approx 1.3862943611","display":true,"kind":"math"}],"index":9,"title":"Time for y=0.5"},{"blocks":[{"content":"Solve y(x)=0.8: 1/(1+4e^{-x})=0.8 â 1+4e^{-x}=1.25 â e^{-x}=0.0625 â x=\\ln 16.","display":true,"kind":"text"},{"content":"\\displaystyle x=\\ln 16\\approx 2.7725887222","display":true,"kind":"math"}],"index":10,"title":"Time for y=0.8"},{"blocks":[{"content":"Verify initial condition by substitution x=0.","display":true,"kind":"text"},{"content":"\\displaystyle y(0)=\\frac{1}{1+4}=\\frac{1}{5}=0.2","display":true,"kind":"math"}],"index":11,"title":"Verify y(0)=0.2"},{"blocks":[{"content":"Plotting instructions: plot y(x)=1/(1+4e^{-x}) on xâ[-5,10], overlay slope field for dy/dx=y(1-y) on a coarse grid, mark x=ln4 (y=0.5) and x=ln16 (y=0.8), and include a phase line with arrows on the y-axis showing stability at y=0 and y=1.","display":true,"kind":"text"}],"index":12,"title":"Plot instructions"}],"question_text":"Q1: Solve the IVP:  dy/dx = y(1 - y),  y(0) = 0.2.\nTasks:\n1) Show the equation is separable.\n2) Separate variables and integrate.\n3) Solve for y(x) explicitly.\n4) Apply y(0)=0.2 to find the constant.\n5) State the final closed-form solution.\n6) Find equilibrium solutions and classify them (stable/unstable).\n7) Determine lim_{xââ} y(x).\n8) Find where the solution has its inflection point (in x).\n9) Compute the time x when y(x)=0.5.\n10) Compute the time x when y(x)=0.8.\n11) Verify y(0)=0.2 by direct substitution into your formula.\n12) Plot y(x) on x â [-5, 10].\n13) Overlay a slope field on the same window (coarse grid acceptable).\n14) Plot the phase line for y' = y(1-y) on the y-axis (direction arrows).\n15) Mark and label the points where y=0.5 and y=0.8 on the solution plot.","task_count":15,"tasks":[{"task_index":1,"task_label":"Show separable"},{"task_index":2,"task_label":"Separate and integrate"},{"task_index":3,"task_label":"Solve explicitly"},{"task_index":4,"task_label":"Apply initial condition"},{"task_index":5,"task_label":"Final solution"},{"task_index":6,"task_label":"Equilibria & stability"},{"task_index":7,"task_label":"Limit as xââ"},{"task_index":8,"task_label":"Inflection point"},{"task_index":9,"task_label":"Time for y=0.5"},{"task_index":10,"task_label":"Time for y=0.8"},{"task_index":11,"task_label":"Verify initial condition"},{"task_index":12,"task_label":"Plot y(x)"},{"task_index":13,"task_label":"Overlay slope field"},{"task_index":14,"task_label":"Phase line"},{"task_index":15,"task_label":"Mark points on plot"}],"question_index":1}],"mode":"step_by_step","request_id":"50bfc163-474b-453a-99a8-4298895a0e51","response_language":"English","schema_name":"youask_math_openai_detailed_v2","schema_version":"v2","tier":"STANDARD"},"created_at":"2026-02-23T10:20:16.440807","model_used":"gpt-5-mini-2025-08-07","tokens_used":10888,"inpu